<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Ait Abbas</h1><p class="st-meta">1510 CE – 1872 CE (approx.) · capital Kalâa of Ait Abbas</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Kabyle mountain kingdom in the Bibans, ruled from the fortress of Kalâa, that long resisted Ottoman Algiers and later led the 1871 Mokrani revolt.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Bejaia</a> in 1510, Hafsid-era notables of the region founded a principality in the Bibans mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesser-kabylia">Lesser Kabylia</a>, with its stronghold at the Kalâa of the Ait Abbas. It controlled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-gates-algeria">Iron Gates</a> pass on the route between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> and Constantine.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom's rulers drew on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabyles">Kabyle</a> tribal levies armed with firearms and on the craft workshops of the Kalâa. Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-aziz">al-Aziz</a>, its most famous ruler, alternately allied with and fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/regency-of-algiers">Regency of Algiers</a> and the rival <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kuku">Kingdom of Kuku</a>, and fell in battle against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> around 1559. Later the ruling family became known as the Mokrani.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Mokrani accommodated Ottoman and then French rule as local lords. In 1871 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohamed-el-mokrani">Mohamed El Mokrani</a> led a great uprising against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-algeria">French Algeria</a>; its defeat in 1872 brought confiscations and the end of the family's power.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1510 CE – 1872 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.75%;width:7.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1510 CE – 1872 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kalâa of Ait Abbas</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd al-Aziz, Mohamed El Mokrani</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kabyle, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ait Abbas, Kalaa of Beni Abbes, Mokrani</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1691&amp;focus=kingdom-of-ait-abbas" aria-label="Kingdom of Ait Abbas on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4795 868 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Ait Abbas lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5115 1124L5255 1107M5115 1124L5077 1108M5115 1124L5077 1108"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5255 1107h0M5077 1108h0M5077 1108h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5115 1124h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5115 1124h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kalâa of Ait Abbas. <a href="/atlas?year=1691&amp;focus=kingdom-of-ait-abbas">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
